      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "While metformin remains the traditional first choice for type 2 diabetes, modern guidelines recommend choosing between SGLT2 inhibitors and GLP-1 receptor agonists as early treatment based on your specific heart, kidney, and weight goals .",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "modern guidelines recommend choosing between SGLT2 inhibitors and GLP-1 receptor agonists as early treatment based on your specific heart, kidney, and weight goals"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "SGLT2 Inhibitors"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What they are: Oral pills taken once daily. Examples include empagliflozin (Jardiance) and dapagliflozin."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "How they work: They help your kidneys remove extra sugar through your urine."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Best for: Patients with heart failure or chronic kidney disease, as they protect heart and kidney function and slow organ damage."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Side effects: Higher risk of genital and urinary tract infections."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "GLP-1 Receptor Agonists"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What they are: Injectable medications (given weekly or daily), though oral options are also available. Examples include semaglutide (Ozempic)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "How they work: They trigger insulin release, stop your liver from making too much sugar, and slow down digestion so you feel full."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Best for: Patients who need significant weight loss or have a high risk of heart attacks and strokes (atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Side effects: Stomach upset, nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "How to Choose"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Choose SGLT2 inhibitors if you have kidney disease or heart failure."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Choose GLP-1 receptor agonists if weight loss and strong blood sugar control are your top priorities."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "You can check to compare copay savings and prescription costs, as both drug classes can be expensive.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "link": "https://www.goodrx.com/conditions/diabetes-type-2/glp-1-vs-sglt2"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help narrow down which option fits you best, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Do you have any heart or kidney conditions ?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Is weight loss a major goal for you?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Do you prefer a daily pill or an injectable medication ?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
